# /etc/cryptobot.env — environment for the cryptobot systemd service.
# Copy to /etc/cryptobot.env (mode 0640, owned by root:ec2-user) on the EC2
# instance. install_remote.sh does this automatically.

# ---- Paths ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repo root. DO NOT EDIT — install_remote.sh force-pins it to $PROJECT_DIR on
# every deploy (:132), because the fallbacks cannot work on the box.
# The next line names the FROZEN remote layout on purpose — that it differs
# from the local tree is precisely why this pin exists.  legacy-path-ok
# The deployed layout is $PROJECT_DIR/src/cryptobot, so config.py's marker-dir
# walk finds neither pyproject.toml nor polymarket/src/cryptobot and would fall
# through to parents[2]. Everything runtime-writable hangs off it (DATA_ROOT -> $_/data,
# LOGS_DIR -> $_/logs), and polymarket.backtest.REPO_ROOT reads the SAME key, so
# repointing it moves both the live engine and any research tooling together —
# which is the point: a producer and its consumer must never end up in
# different trees.
CRYPTOBOT_ROOT=/home/ec2-user/cryptobot
PYTHONPATH=/home/ec2-user/cryptobot/src
# Suppress a noisy sklearn internal parallel warning that can otherwise flood
# scanner.err during 1Hz live scoring.
PYTHONWARNINGS=ignore::UserWarning:sklearn.utils.parallel
CRYPTOBOT_DB_PATH=/home/ec2-user/cryptobot/data/cryptobot.db
# The current Polymarket source contract is
# `polymarket/live/config/twap_symmetric_live.json`; deploy.sh stages it under
# this remote compatibility filename. install_remote.sh force-pins it every
# deploy. The TWAP model lives under data/models/twap_symmetric_v1/.
CRYPTOBOT_V6_CONFIG=/home/ec2-user/cryptobot/runtime/config/v2_step1last_live.json
CRYPTOBOT_DASHBOARD_DIR=/home/ec2-user/cryptobot/dashboard

# ---- Cadence ----------------------------------------------------------------
CRYPTOBOT_TICK_SECONDS=1
CRYPTOBOT_SPOT_SOURCE=binance
# Direct TWAP-symmetric scorer (Polymarket only). It requires both Chainlink's
# signed boundary TWAP and a causal Binance 60s opening TWAP; either missing
# anchor abstains instead of falling back to the cross-source point ratio.
CRYPTOBOT_TWAP_SYMMETRIC_ENABLED=1
CRYPTOBOT_TWAP_RTDS_URL=wss://ws-live-data.polymarket.com
CRYPTOBOT_SPOT_FETCH_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1
# Match BT's Binance 1-second kline-close spot contract (deploy pins 1).
CRYPTOBOT_SPOT_USE_1S_KLINES=0
CRYPTOBOT_SPOT_STALENESS_S=5
CRYPTOBOT_BINANCE_BASE_URL=https://data-api.binance.vision
# A7 spot prefetch lead — the prefetch daemon fetches the spot batch this many ms
# before each second boundary. Measured Binance fetch from the box is ~204ms, so
# the config default 200ms lead LOSES the race every tick (trace 2026-07-10) and
# the tick pays the inline fetch; 450ms wins it. Spot is a 1s bucket so the
# fetched VALUE is unchanged — only the race timing moves. install_remote.sh
# force-pins this; SPOT_PREFETCH_ENABLED stays default-on.
CRYPTOBOT_SPOT_PREFETCH_LEAD_MS=450
# Phase B parallel order POST (latency lever). DEFAULT OFF. When ON and >=2
# place-candidate LIVE cells reach the order-POST stage in one tick, their
# ~250ms venue round trips fire CONCURRENTLY on a transient thread pool instead
# of serially — so N LIVE POSTs in a tick cost ~250ms of decision->fill latency
# instead of ~N*250ms (saving ~250ms per EXTRA cell; the common multi-coin
# 15m-boundary tick posts 3-4 at once). Pre-POST (gates -> walk -> sizing ->
# reserve) stays strictly serial in cell order and post-POST processing (ledger
# writes/telemetry) is serial in cell order; only the network POST is parallel.
# RISK / behavioral divergence: reserved cells apply their stake to the
# within-tick exposure deltas PESSIMISTICALLY at reserve time, so a later cell's
# gate counts an earlier reserved bet even if that POST later rejects —
# conservative (never over-exposes), but slightly tighter than the serial path
# which only counts ACCEPTED fills. Also, an earlier LIVE cell's ledger row is
# not written until after the loop, so same-tick DB dedup can't see it (benign
# here: within one tick a sleeve has one entry_minute per coin, the
# uniq_loa_active_slot index still blocks true same-slot double-reservation, and
# the ask-bands are disjoint). Leave OFF unless multi-cell POST latency is the
# measured bottleneck.
# CRYPTOBOT_PHASE_B_PARALLEL_POST=1
# V2_EDGE_CAP — pred_edge upper cap, REGISTERED CANDIDATE (2026-07-22), OFF by
# default and force-pinned 0 by install_remote.sh until the pre-registered
# 2-week live grade passes. Evidence: claimed edge is anti-calibrated at the
# top — live 0.08-0.10 = -3.1c/$ (n=47), 0.10+ = -44.1c/$ (WR 36% vs claimed
# 87%); fold-F at-ask replay 0.06-0.08 -6.2 / 0.08-0.10 -16.0 / 0.10+ -23.7
# c/$. When >0 the v6 loader clamps sleeve max_edge = min(artifact, cap) and
# the existing edge_above_ceiling gate skips those entries (signals telemetry
# = the graded cohort). Candidate arm values: 0.06 (fold-F optimal) or 0.08
# (conservative, negative in live and both folds).
# CRYPTOBOT_V2_EDGE_CAP=0
# v2 promotion: topups OFF so each market/resolution gets exactly ONE order.
CRYPTOBOT_ENABLE_TOPUPS=0
CRYPTOBOT_SWEEP_MINUTES=5
CRYPTOBOT_SIGNALS_RETENTION_DAYS=7
# Live-equity floor. The 2026-05-23 free-size portfolio backtest targets
# about 0.0481 bankroll (5m) and 0.0189 bankroll (15m), so both clear the $1
# minimum with the default $100 bankroll and the 2026-07 live $120.3838 seed.
CRYPTOBOT_MIN_BET_USD=1.0
# Exposure cap and DD halt MUST equal the deployed artifact's
# concurrent_exposure_cap_fraction / max_drawdown_halt_frac
# (v2_step1last_live.json) or the loader's drift-check fails closed at boot.
# Both are 1.0 / 0.30 in the v2 artifact — this env MUST match (1.0 / 0.30).
# NOTE: omit both to use the config.py defaults (1.0 / 0.30).
# Risk retune (operator-ordered 2026-07-21): halt 0.35 -> 0.40, paired with
# the brake retune below (scale 0.60 = half size at >=30% DD).
# THROTTLE REMOVAL (operator-ordered 2026-07-31): halt 0.40 -> 0.30. With the
# graduated brake below now inert and both intervals flat at 1%, this halt is
# the ONLY drawdown guard; the deployed both-hold twin's worst-fold backtest
# maxDD is 26.6%. See
# polymarket/backtest/studies/tick_latency/THROTTLE_REMOVAL_SIZE_20260731.md.
CRYPTOBOT_SHARED_EXPOSURE_CAP=1.0
CRYPTOBOT_MAX_DD_HALT_FRAC=0.30
# Polymarket deploys override the shared default above to 0.40 in
# install_remote.sh; predict.fun keeps 0.30.
# ---- v2 "step1last" equity-fraction sizing ----------------------------------
# Per-bet stake = equity * base_frac(interval) * brake(dd) * conc_weight(k),
# floored UP to CRYPTOBOT_MIN_BET_USD. Brake = max(BRAKE_FLOOR, 1 - dd/BRAKE_SCALE);
# concurrency downweight = 1/sqrt(k) when CONC_DOWNWEIGHT=1. The DD halt above
# is the terminal stop; the brake USED to be a graduated throttle beneath it
# (scale 0.60 / floor 0.50 = half size at >=30% DD, risk retune 2026-07-21).
# Current TWAP production sizing is 2% on both intervals. install_remote.sh
# force-pins these values for the Polymarket role.
CRYPTOBOT_V2_BASE_FRAC_15M=0.020
CRYPTOBOT_V2_BASE_FRAC_5M=0.020
CRYPTOBOT_V2_BRAKE_SCALE=0.60
CRYPTOBOT_V2_BRAKE_FLOOR=1.0
CRYPTOBOT_V2_CONC_DOWNWEIGHT=1
# F2 tier-A size boost (2026-07-14): stake x MULT when the PLACE is the
# market's FIRST qualifying second AND the score edge >= EDGE. MULT=1.0 disables.
CRYPTOBOT_V2_TIER_A_MULT=1.0
CRYPTOBOT_V2_TIER_A_EDGE=0.0465
# Depth cap REMOVED (operator order 2026-07-11): stakes are pure equity-fraction
# sizing, no per-coin USD ceiling. The CRYPTOBOT_V2_DEPTH_CAP_* and the old
# CRYPTOBOT_V2_MULTIFILL_MAX keys are dead (the entry ceiling came back below as
# CRYPTOBOT_V2_MULTIFILL_MAX_EXTRA, which counts EXTRAS, not a total).
# EVERY-QUALIFYING ENTRIES — ARMED (operator order 2026-07-25). MIN_EQUITY 5000
# -> 0 makes multifill live at the current ~$130 equity, so the entry rule moves
# from "the first qualifying bet owns the resolution" to "every qualifying bet":
# once the first attempt FILLS, each later qualifying second is a fresh
# independent entry re-scored on a fresh book/prob.
# MAX_EXTRA 3 = 1 initial + 3 extras = at most 4 non-topup ledger rows per
# (coin, interval, window). REQUIRED alongside the 0 floor: a 15m window offers
# 30 qualifying seconds, so uncapped a resolution could stack ~30 entries ~= $97
# at ~$130 equity — ~75% of the bankroll on ONE binary. The exposure cap does not
# bound that (cap_tracks_equity: its ceiling IS equity, so it caps TOTAL
# exposure, never per-market concentration). Capped: ~$13, ~10%. A bound entry
# records skip_reason='multifill_cap'. Also bounded by the same-side rule (never
# both legs of one binary) and the DD brake (inert since 2026-07-31) + 30% halt.
# Disarm = MIN_EQUITY 5000, or MAX_EXTRA 0 (one entry per resolution), or
# *_ENABLED=0. All env-only, no redeploy needed.
# ⛔ CORRECTED 2026-07-25 (same day): MULTIFILL OFF. It is the WRONG mechanism
# for "every qualifying" — it opens INDEPENDENT extra ENTRIES after a fill, so
# one resolution took 4 entries + 2 T3 top-ups = 6 orders. Intended shape is ONE
# entry retried every qualifying second UNTIL IT FILLS (retries write no ledger
# row, so they never multiply positions), then <=3 top-ups on that one position
# => <=4 orders per resolution. V2_REJECT_RETRY + V2_RETRY_REPRICE already give
# the retry-until-fill behavior; multifill is not needed for it.
CRYPTOBOT_V2_MULTIFILL_ENABLED=0
CRYPTOBOT_V2_MULTIFILL_MIN_EQUITY=0
CRYPTOBOT_V2_MULTIFILL_MAX_EXTRA=3
# The top-up half: disabled after the 2026-08-15 live audit. Keep the state
# machine available for research, but do not place new scale-in orders.
CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_ENABLED=0
CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_MAX_N=3
# 5m INTERVAL — RE-ENABLED LIVE (operator order 2026-07-29), under the
# first-attempt-only regime with every-qualifying entry selection, i.e. the same
# semantics as 15m. install_remote.sh FORCE-PINS this key to 1 on every deploy
# (set_env_line CRYPTOBOT_INTERVAL_5M_ENABLED "1"), so the value seeded from this
# example file is inert — the box always ends up at 1 regardless of what is
# written here. Change the pin in install_remote.sh, not this line.
# The gate itself is ENTRY-only: at 0 no 5m sleeve may open a NEW entry (the tick
# loop skips them silently — no signal rows, no API calls) but subminute_5m stays
# in the loaded portfolio, so open 5m positions keep stop-loss coverage and the
# dashboard keeps showing 5m history and PnL.
# History: 5m was DISABLED 2026-07-25 as the bleeder (clean-era regrade had
# subminute_5m at -6.4c/$1 on 82% of the mass vs subminute_15m at +12.5c/$1); the
# 07-29 re-enable is an explicit operator override of that data.
CRYPTOBOT_INTERVAL_5M_ENABLED=1
# Current production universe: BTC+ETH+SOL+XRP. The TWAP loader rejects any mismatch
# between this value, the live contract, and the model manifest.
CRYPTOBOT_COINS=BTC,ETH,SOL,XRP
# Revert (env-only, no redeploy): point CRYPTOBOT_V6_CONFIG at a different
# v6-format artifact AND set the cap + DD halt to THAT artifact's
# concurrent_exposure_cap_fraction / max_drawdown_halt_frac — the loader's
# drift-check requires the trio to agree, so all three must flip together.
# Set by install_remote.sh on first wallet deploy to cut dry-run accounting
# over from that UTC timestamp without deleting historical ledger rows.
# CRYPTOBOT_WALLET_START_AT=2026-05-23 00:00:00

# ---- Dashboard / SSE binding ------------------------------------------------
# 127.0.0.1 = loopback only (safe). Access via SSH tunnel:
#   ssh -L 8800:127.0.0.1:8800 -i polymarket/cryptobot.pem ec2-user@<ec2-host>
#   then open http://127.0.0.1:8800/ locally.
#
# To bind 0.0.0.0 (public) you ALSO need CRYPTOBOT_ALLOW_REMOTE_DASHBOARD=1
# AND CRYPTOBOT_DASHBOARD_TLS_TERMINATED=1 (confirms a TLS-terminating reverse
# proxy — nginx + basic auth, Cloudflare Access, Tailscale — sits in front).
# Boot fails fast if non-loopback bind is requested without both flags set.
CRYPTOBOT_DASHBOARD_HOST=127.0.0.1
CRYPTOBOT_DASHBOARD_PORT=8800
# CRYPTOBOT_ALLOW_REMOTE_DASHBOARD=0
# CRYPTOBOT_DASHBOARD_TLS_TERMINATED=0

# ---- Dashboard cookie auth (REQUIRED before any wallet flips LIVE) ----------
# do_POST handler reads these on every mode-flip / operator-control / transfer
# request. Cookie is set to SameSite=Strict for CSRF protection. DASHBOARD_PASS
# MUST be a long random string (>= 32 chars); short or empty passes fail boot.
CRYPTOBOT_DASHBOARD_USER=admin
CRYPTOBOT_DASHBOARD_PASS=

# ---- Polymarket CLOB credentials (REQUIRED for LIVE mode) -------------------
# Get fresh creds for THIS wallet — DO NOT reuse hightempbot's creds.
# Generate via Polymarket UI or `python -m cryptobot_polymarket.derive_creds`.
# All four required to place orders; read-only book + price queries don't
# need any of them.
POLY_API_KEY=
POLY_SECRET=
POLY_PASSPHRASE=
POLY_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ---- Polymarket V2 wallet topology ------------------------------------------
# POLY_SIGNATURE_TYPE: 0=EOA, 1=POLY_PROXY (legacy), 2=POLY_GNOSIS_SAFE,
#                     3=POLY_1271 (standard "deposit wallet" — most users).
# MetaMask users: SIG depends on funds location, not signer choice.
#   - Polymarket Deposit page shows a DIFFERENT address than MetaMask → SIG=3,
#     POLY_FUNDER = that deposit address (Polymarket-managed smart contract).
#   - Same address as MetaMask → SIG=0, POLY_FUNDER = MetaMask address.
# When SIG=3, POLY_FUNDER is REQUIRED. Boot refuses to start otherwise.
# Cryptobot uses its OWN deposit wallet — do NOT paste hightempbot's funder.
# Fund the deposit wallet before flipping any wallet to LIVE. The live config is a
# single shared-equity wallet group (group_live, cap $120.3838 = the full
# funded balance; sub-minute members are flag-stripped when disabled).
POLY_SIGNATURE_TYPE=3
POLY_FUNDER=
POLY_RETURN_WALLET=

# ---- Polymarket relayer (transfer + redemption submissions) -----------------
RELAYER_URL=https://relayer-v2.polymarket.com
RELAYER_API_KEY=
RELAYER_API_KEY_ADDRESS=

# ---- Polygon RPC (on-chain wallet/CTF reconciliation) -----------------------
POLYGON_RPC_URL=https://polygon-rpc.com

# ---- Live readiness / wallet reconciliation TTLs ----------------------------
LIVE_REQUIRE_DEPOSIT_WALLET=true
LIVE_ONCHAIN_VERIFY_ENABLED=true
LIVE_BALANCE_TOLERANCE_USD=0.25
WALLET_SNAPSHOT_FRESHNESS_TTL_S=900
WALLET_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL_MINUTES=10
# Auto-redeem RETIRED 2026-08-04: Polymarket NATIVE redeem handles claims. The
# bot-side redeemer and its AUTO_REDEEM_* keys were deleted from the codebase;
# setting them here does nothing.

# ---- Mode + bankroll --------------------------------------------------------
# DRY_RUN sets the DEFAULT mode for fresh wallets on first boot only. Once
# wallet_mode_state has rows, per-wallet mode is authoritative (toggled via
# dashboard or `python -m cryptobot.cli.set_wallet_mode`).
# Live accounting seed. When changing this to the current CLOB pUSD balance,
# also reset CRYPTOBOT_WALLET_START_AT to the cutover timestamp so historical
# PnL is not added on top of the new wallet balance. The research artifact
# itself remains pinned to bankroll=100.
CRYPTOBOT_INITIAL_BANKROLL=100
DRY_RUN=true

# ---- Telegram alerts (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# NOTIFY_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=
# NOTIFY_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ---- Sub-minute checkpoint sleeves (v2 "step1last" — 100% of live) ----------
# Note: the legacy sleeve IDs exp044_5m/exp044_15m are retained as live DB
# identifiers (wallet-group members) even though ORB/exp044 was retired — do
# not rename them. The live sleeves are subminute_5m/subminute_15m.
# Master flag. v2 promotion REQUIRES this ON: with it off the v6 loader drops
# the subminute_5m/subminute_15m sleeves and the checkpoint-only v2 config has
# nothing to run (fails closed). install_remote.sh force-pins it to 1 on every
# deploy. Rollback = git revert the ORB/exp044 removal + redeploy.
CRYPTOBOT_SUBMINUTE_ENABLED=1
# STOP-LOSS RETIRED (operator order 2026-08-05). The PURE_STOP_04 model
# stop-loss EXIT is DELETED from the engine. It was already inert in production:
# CRYPTOBOT_STOPLOSS_EXCLUDE_INTERVALS was pinned "5,15", exempting BOTH traded
# intervals, so no position could be sold by it. Every filled position now HOLDs
# to binary settlement. Retired keys (install_remote.sh scrubs them from
# /etc/cryptobot.env so a stale pin cannot shadow a future knob of the same
# name): CRYPTOBOT_STOPLOSS_{ENABLED,BAND,MAX_ATTEMPTS,SELL_CHASE,
# EXCLUDE_INTERVALS,MIN_EXIT_VALUE_USD}, CRYPTOBOT_STOP_SLIP_EXEMPT{,_THRESH},
# CRYPTOBOT_MIN_STOPPABLE_STAKE_USD.
#
# Historical ledger rows closed by the old stop (outcome='CANCELLED',
# exit_kind='stop_loss', exit_ts/exit_price set) remain valid and still render —
# neither the exit_kind column nor the stop_loss_attempts table was dropped.
# Nothing writes them any more.
#
# The per-second held-position loop SURVIVES as the T3 scale-in driver
# (execution/held_position_pass.py). Its two book knobs were RENAMED:
#   CRYPTOBOT_STOPLOSS_BOOK_CHAIN    -> CRYPTOBOT_HELD_PASS_BOOK_CHAIN
#   CRYPTOBOT_STOPLOSS_BATCH_BOOKS   -> CRYPTOBOT_HELD_PASS_BATCH_BOOKS
#   CRYPTOBOT_STOPLOSS_FAST_CADENCE_MS -> CRYPTOBOT_HELD_PASS_CADENCE_MS
# and the old model-stop band lives on as the T3 model-deterioration DISARM band
# (see CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_DISARM_BAND below).
#
# Held-position book-source chain (install_remote.sh force-pins 1). Routes the
# pass's two per-candidate book reads through the shared WS/prefetch chain
# instead of raw REST GETs. Fail-closed: no chain wired => byte-identical REST.
# CRYPTOBOT_HELD_PASS_BOOK_CHAIN=1
# Batched book reads (latency lever; DEFAULT ON). The pass's two authoritative
# REST book reads per candidate (held + other token) arrive in ONE batched
# POST /books instead of two serial per-token GETs (same parser either way;
# per-token GETs remain the fallback when the batch fails or omits a token).
# Kill switch: 0 skips the batch attempt entirely and restores the per-token GET
# path byte-identically.
# CRYPTOBOT_HELD_PASS_BATCH_BOOKS=1
# Held-position pass cadence (latency lever). DEFAULT 0 = the pass runs INLINE in
# the 1Hz tick, strictly after Phase B (so a top-up never sits between an entry
# decision and its POST). When > 0 (MILLISECONDS, clamped UP to a 250ms floor —
# the Polymarket taker delay makes a tighter loop pointless) the inline pass is
# SKIPPED and a DEDICATED scheduler job runs it at this cadence on its own
# connection, decoupling T3 top-ups from entry timing. A fire that lands between
# an entry's ledger commit and its deferred fill write-back sees the position's
# fill still NULL and simply skips it until the next cycle (no crash). Requires
# SCALEIN_T3_ENABLED (the pass self-gates on it).
# CRYPTOBOT_HELD_PASS_CADENCE_MS=250
#
# T3 scale-in taker top-ups (research WFO pick 2026-07-15; SCALEIN_GRID_DIGEST.md
# — digest removed in a6df8ed; recover via `git show
# a6df8ed^:polymarket/backtest/studies/tick_latency/SCALEIN_GRID_DIGEST.md`).
# After a sub-minute entry fills, scale into the SAME side with small
# frozen-at-entry FAK top-ups while the market "has not dipped". Rides inside the
# per-second held-position loop (execution/scale_in.py, driven from
# execution/held_position_pass.py), so it adds no new network fetch and requires
# SUBMINUTE_ENABLED=1 (it only acts on sub-minute LIVE fills). Each second, one
# FAK top-up on the held side while ALL hold: (i) no-dip — the side ask has never
# been observed below the entry ask; (ii) the WALKED ask for the stake <= CAP
# (0.83); (iii) spread <= SPREAD_MAX (0.02); (iv) fewer than MAX_N (3) top-up
# FILLS; (v) cumulative top-up fill cash + this stake <= EXPOSURE_CAP (1.5x) of
# the entry's realized fill; (vi) all existing entry risk checks (40% DD halt,
# available cash, $1 floor) — the top-up cash flows through the same ledger
# accounting (a PENDING LIVE row tagged scalein_topup=1). Stake = FRAC (0.5x) the
# entry's requested stake; limit = own walked_limit + FAK_PAD (0.01) capped 0.99
# (NOT the entry's anchored pad).
#
# DISARM: top-ups stop permanently for a market on the first no-dip violation,
# and on model DETERIORATION — the ex-PURE_STOP_04 predicate, which fires when
# the re-scored bid >= model_p + DISARM_BAND while the position is underwater.
# That predicate no longer sells anything (the stop-loss exit is retired); its
# only effect is this disarm. Band FROZEN at 0.04 (scalp_digest.md § C/D LOCKED,
# formerly CRYPTOBOT_STOPLOSS_BAND); do not tune without re-running the
# delay-stress.
#
# DEFAULT OFF in code. install_remote.sh does NOT pin this flag — to arm it,
# the operator adds CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_ENABLED=1 (and any non-default knob) to
# /etc/cryptobot.env directly and restarts the service. install_remote.sh only
# rewrites keys it explicitly set_env_line's, so a manually-added key persists
# across deploys.
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_ENABLED=0
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_MAX_N=3
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_DISARM_BAND=0.04
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_FRAC=0.5
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_NO_DIP=0.0
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_CAP=0.83
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_SPREAD_MAX=0.02
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_EXPOSURE_CAP=1.5
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_CADENCE_S=1
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_FAK_PAD=0.01
# CRYPTOBOT_SCALEIN_T3_END_BUFFER_S=4
#
# Top-up edge floor (DEFAULT 0.0 is ACTIVE, not off — 2026-07-23 incident,
# venue-independent). Live id7: a T3 scale-in top-up chased 5c above its 0.75
# anchor and filled at 0.81 with recorded realized_edge -0.0119 — the top-up
# paths re-price their edge but only enforced the V2_EDGE_CAP CEILING, never
# a floor. A top-up whose recomputed edge is < the floor is SKIPPED, using
# the SAME edge quantity each path already records: T3 scale-in rejects
# 'edge_below_floor' on the re-priced add-on edge; generic within-minute
# top-ups skip 'topup_edge_below_floor' in the gate stack. Strict <, so an
# edge of exactly the floor passes; 0.0 blocks exactly the negative-edge
# cohort (orders that contradict the sizing logic's own claim) and nothing
# else. Entries are never touched.
# CRYPTOBOT_TOPUP_EDGE_FLOOR=0.0
#
# T3 same-second "blind" top-up fresh gate (tri-state, DEFAULT "0" = OFF =
# byte-identical). A top-up placed in the SAME SECOND as its parent ENTRY is
# blind: the stop pass drives the top-up scan inside the same 1s tick as the
# entry, against a held-side book that can PREDATE the parent's POST, so a book
# crashing onto the parent in-flight (250ms uncancellable taker delay) is not yet
# observable and the no-dip check cannot see it — the top-up buys the same crater
# (real case 2026-07-20: ETH parent + top-up both stamped 14:34:54, decision ask
# 0.69, both filled 0.60). Live ledger since 07-14: same-second top-ups n=50 ->
# -$5.81 total; top-ups placed >=1s after the parent n=117 -> +$4.28. The gate
# kills only the blind cohort and leaves the later cohort untouched.
#
# Rule: require the scan second to be STRICTLY after the parent's fill second
# (reject when now_epoch <= parent_fill_epoch), parsed from live_fill_ts then
# bet_ts then created_at. A book RECV timestamp would be better evidence but is
# unavailable (BookSnapshot.fetched_at_ts is LOCAL fetch time on REST, audit
# #12). This also RESTORES live<->backtest parity: the T3 reference
# (tick_topup_foldBE._simulate_topups) starts its first top-up at
# t = ceil(entry_fill_ts) + 1, so it never simulates the same-second top-up live
# currently allows. A live skip is a DELAY, not a kill — it consumes no cadence
# throttle and never disarms, so the next second's scan proceeds normally.
# FAIL-OPEN: if no timestamp parses at all the top-up is ALLOWED (T3 is +EV
# overall and must never be silently killed by a data gap).
# Tri-state: "0"=off, "shadow"=log+count only ("topup fresh-gate shadow:
# would_skip ledger_id=..." — the top-up still PROCEEDS; grade offline by joining
# the logged ledger_id to its settlement pnl_net), "1"=live skip (debug reason
# `fresh_gate`). Shadow-first enable path: run "shadow" for ~3 weeks (or until
# the would_skip cohort is large enough to grade), confirm the same-second cohort
# is still the losing one, then flip to "1".
# CRYPTOBOT_TOPUP_FRESH_GATE=0
#
# A8 REST book prefetch-ahead: a daemon re-fetches the previous tick's
# POST /books token set ~LEAD_MS before each second boundary; the tick reads
# those snapshots (served only if younger than MAX_AGE_MS) instead of paying
# the inline batch round-trip. Any miss falls through to the inline fetch, so
# the failure mode is the legacy behavior. Armed on the box by install_remote.sh.
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_PREFETCH_ENABLED=true
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_PREFETCH_LEAD_MS=150
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_PREFETCH_MAX_AGE_MS=700
#
# WS book mirror: mirror the CLOB *market* WebSocket channel into a snapshot
# cache the tick reads before the inline POST /books. The WS book carries a
# server timestamp so book staleness becomes real (audit #12). On any WS
# error/disconnect the mirror serves nothing and the tick falls back to REST.
# MAX_AGE_MS matches the REST prefetch bound (700) — a book older than that can
# price a limit that FAK-rejects. NOW ARMED IN SHADOW (operator order
# 2026-07-10); arm procedure has three steps:
#   (1) Shadow [ACTIVE NOW]: BOTH ENABLED=1 and SHADOW=1. The mirror runs and
#       compares but REST stays authoritative for every decision; watch the
#       WS/REST divergence counters (the "book WS shadow divergence" log) for
#       >=1 clean day.
#   (2) Authoritative: after >=1 clean day at ~0 divergence, drop SHADOW (leave
#       ENABLED=1) — the mirror now serves books first.
#   (3) Kill switch: set ENABLED=0 (or unset) to fall straight back to REST.
# install_remote.sh force-pins ENABLED=1 + SHADOW=1 on every deploy.
CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_ENABLED=1
CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_SHADOW=0
# Freshness gate: serve a mirror snapshot only if younger than this at
# decision time; older falls back to the REST batch. EFFECTIVELY REMOVED
# 2026-08-06 (operator): snapshot age = market quietness, not feed lag (the
# venue pushes changes at ~1ms inter-frame), so the gate only ever traded
# ~119-200ms REST round trips for protection against a stalled-but-connected
# subscription — a risk the operator accepted. 600000 (10 min) outlives every
# market window. install_remote.sh force-pins this on the polymarket role.
CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_MAX_AGE_MS=600000
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_URL=wss://ws-subscriptions-clob.polymarket.com/ws/market
#
# -- WS orphan fix (2026-07-25 latency audit) ---------------------------------
# Measured on the live box: the venue market channel pushes ~822 msg/s with a
# p50 1ms inter-frame gap on the open *-updown-* windows, while the mirror was
# serving DECISION books with a p50 age of 6,935ms (max 114,498ms) and its recv
# thread sat at ~3% of one core — the feed is a firehose, the consumer was
# barely reading it. Cause: cache entries for tokens that rolled out of the
# window were never evicted, and get()'s only gate is CONNECTION-level
# recv-liveness (re-stamped by ANY frame, including pings and other tokens'
# subscription acks), so a two-windows-old ladder priced live FAKs.
#
# EVICT_UNSUBSCRIBED (default 1 = ON): drop a token's cached ladder the moment
# it leaves the subscribed set. Can only ever REMOVE stale data — the fallback
# is the well-tested REST batch. Set 0 only to reproduce pre-fix behavior.
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_EVICT_UNSUBSCRIBED=1
#
# MAX_BOOK_AGE_MS (default 0 = OFF): per-token venue-book age gate, measured on
# the SAME quantity the Latency tab shows as book age. This is the SAFETY NET,
# not the fix — with eviction on, ages collapse and it should rarely fire.
# ⚠️ Do NOT arm this at ~400ms while ages are still seconds-scale: it would
# reject essentially every WS hit, which is equivalent to (and slower than)
# just setting CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_ENABLED=0.
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_MAX_BOOK_AGE_MS=0
#
# -- WS mirror STALL WATCHDOG (operator order 2026-08-06) ---------------------
# Lineage: MAX_AGE_MS above was effectively removed because snapshot age on
# these books = market QUIETNESS, not feed lag. The accepted residual risk is
# the gray zone the mirror cannot see by itself — a STALLED-BUT-CONNECTED
# subscription (socket alive, so recv-liveness keeps being re-stamped by pings
# and other tokens' frames, while updates for ONE subscribed token silently
# stop) would price a dead ladder until the window rolls. Connection death
# already clears the mirror; a rolled-off token is evicted by the orphan fix
# above. This watchdog covers what is left.
#
# It runs ONLY on the scheduler pool — never on the tick/order path, so the WS
# hot path is unchanged. Each pass takes the mirror's serving set, keeps the
# tokens whose ladder is older than STALL_SUSPECT_MS (oldest first, capped at
# MAX_TOKENS_PER_PASS), asks the venue for those books in ONE batch POST, and
# compares TOP-OF-BOOK: price must match exactly, size within SIZE_REL_TOL.
# MATCH => stamped verified (not re-asked for VERIFY_TTL_MS unless new ws
# activity lands first) so a quiet-but-correct book is not re-fetched every
# pass. MISMATCH => the token is evicted from the mirror, so the next entry-path
# read falls through to REST truth, and a WARNING is logged with both books; the
# mirror repopulates it on the next full `book` frame. Any REST error/timeout is
# a silent skip — a failed verify NEVER evicts.
#
# REST budget: at most ONE POST /books per pass = 12/min at the default 5s.
# ENABLED default 1 (armed wherever the mirror is authoritative: BOOK_WS_ENABLED
# and SHADOW=0). Set 0 to construct nothing and register no job.
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_WATCHDOG_ENABLED=1
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_S=5
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_WATCHDOG_STALL_SUSPECT_MS=5000
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_WATCHDOG_MAX_TOKENS_PER_PASS=4
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_WATCHDOG_VERIFY_TTL_MS=30000
# CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_WATCHDOG_SIZE_REL_TOL=0.02
# Counters ride the Latency tab's book-freshness panel (tooltip on the book-age
# tile; visible text only once there has been an eviction).
#
# -- RF step-function LUT (2026-07-25 latency audit) --------------------------
# Serves the univariate checkpoint_rf forests from an exact step-function
# lookup table (sorted breakpoints + searchsorted) instead of 200 tree traversals:
# 0.003ms vs ~6.8ms measured, and score_cell_hgb calls predict_proba once per
# cell (~5.3 cells/tick), so this was ~36ms of every order tick. Bit-exact — validated over 41,480 adversarial probes (0 mismatches),
# thresholds snapped DOWN to float32 because sklearn casts X to float32 before the
# float64 `x <= threshold` test. Built on a daemon thread; a slice serves the
# unchanged sklearn path until its LUT lands, and NaN z always falls back.
# Default ON. Set 0 to force sklearn everywhere WITHOUT a redeploy — this is the
# only change in the pass that alters a number the decision reads.
# CRYPTOBOT_RF_STEP_LUT=1
#
# Fix 3a — pre-POST freshness recheck (flag-gated, DEFAULT OFF = byte-identical).
# The FAK limit is priced from the correct-side book read ONCE per tick and never
# re-read before the order POST; the level can vanish in the gap (maker pull,
# intra-tick serial Phase-B work, a 700ms-old prefetch/WS frame), so the FAK
# crosses a gone book and rejects (no_liquidity). When ENABLED, the pipeline
# re-reads the correct-side token from the SAME WS/prefetch source right before
# reserving the LIVE order and, if a fresh re-walk no longer covers MIN_COVER_FRAC
# of the sized stake, SKIPS the POST (writes a `prepost_recheck_skip` signal, no
# reserve, no POST, window NOT consumed — the next qualifying second re-tries).
# SKIP variant only. FAIL-OPEN: no source / no fresh frame => proceed exactly as
# today. LIVE sub-minute (offset) cells only. Validate FIRST in shadow (leave this
# OFF, keep BOOK_WS_ENABLED=1 + BOOK_WS_SHADOW=1): each would-POST logs what the
# gate WOULD decide vs the real fill/reject ("prepost_recheck shadow: ...").
# Enable-live gate: >=90% true-positive over >=3 days.
# CRYPTOBOT_PREPOST_RECHECK_ENABLED=0
# Skip when re-walked coverable < proposed_bet_size * this (1.0 = require full
# coverage; lower to tolerate a partially-thinned book).
# CRYPTOBOT_PREPOST_RECHECK_MIN_COVER_FRAC=1.0
#
# Fix 3a drop-guard extension — pre-POST TOXIC-drop guard (tri-state, DEFAULT
# "0" = OFF = byte-identical). The recheck above only catches the MISS direction
# (book thinned). This catches the TOXIC direction: between the Pass-2 book read
# and the POST the fresh best ask DROPPED >= THRESH below the decision-time ask
# (the book is collapsing mid-flight, so the FAK fills BELOW the decision ask — a
# validated -EV "toxic" fill; the 2026-07-19 study puts the damage floor at 0.02
# below decision ask, and the -0.02..-0.01 slip bucket is actually +EV, so 0.02
# is the floor — do NOT block 1c wiggles). Rides the SAME fresh re-read as the
# cover recheck. Tri-state: "0"=off, "shadow"=count-only (logs+classifies each
# would-abort with the decision+fresh ask for offline ledger grading, NEVER
# suppresses), "1"=live abort (skip_reason `prepost_drop_skip`, window NOT
# consumed). Cover guard takes precedence if both fire. Shadow-first enable path:
# run "shadow" for >=3 days (keep BOOK_WS_ENABLED=1), grade the true-abort rate
# offline, then flip to "1".
# CRYPTOBOT_PREPOST_DROP_GUARD=0
# Minimum drop (decision_ask - fresh_ask, price units) that trips the guard.
# 0.02 = the validated damage floor; do NOT lower below ~0.02 without re-validating.
# CRYPTOBOT_PREPOST_DROP_GUARD_THRESH=0.02
#
# Late-window entry skip gate (flag-gated, DEFAULT "" = {} = OFF = byte-
# identical). Per-coin cutoff (seconds before window close) below which a LIVE
# sub-minute entry is dropped as a validated -EV cohort. Format: comma list of
# COIN:SECONDS. Validated 2026-07-19 study: BTC entries in the LAST 20s of a
# window net +$34.93/era when SKIPPED (split-half validated in BOTH directions),
# so the canonical pin is "BTC:20". Multiple coins: "BTC:20,ETH:10". Coins are
# upper-cased; malformed tokens (no colon, blank coin, non-int/negative seconds)
# are IGNORED so one typo can neither wipe the map nor suppress a live order.
# LIVE offset cells only — DRY paper rows + minute-boundary cells are untouched
# (research parity). No reserve, no POST, window NOT consumed (the next second
# re-evaluates), just a `late_window_skip` signal.
# History: force-pinned BTC:20 on 2026-07-21, REMOVED (and deploy-time scrubbed)
# by operator order 2026-07-23, RE-ARMED at 5s on all four coins by operator
# order 2026-08-01 — install_remote.sh force-pins the value below, so a
# hand-added env line will NOT survive a deploy either way.
# Current pin rationale (project_late_window_loss_20260801): entries with <=10s
# left carry 87% of the era loss (−$37.63 / 214 bets, p≈1e-7), live and the
# fill-corrected tick twin agreeing; <=5s is the robust half (18/19 weeks,
# 16/16 walk-forward), <=10s is outlier-sensitive and stays unarmed.
# ⚠ raw at-ask backtests rank this cohort BACKWARDS (ghost fills) — grade only
# against the fill-corrected pool. Kill switch = set this to "" and redeploy.
CRYPTOBOT_LATE_WINDOW_SKIP=BTC:5,ETH:5,SOL:5,XRP:5
#
# Ask-band entry skip gate (flag-gated, DEFAULT "" = () = OFF = byte-identical).
# Drops an entry whose DECISION-TIME ask (the same top-of-book scalar the sleeve
# band test, the gate stack and the signals `ask` column use) lands inside a
# per-(coin, sleeve) band measured to have gone adverse. Format: comma list of
# COIN:SLEEVE:LO-HI.
#   * COIN   — case-insensitive (upper-cased).
#   * SLEEVE — PREFIX match on the sleeve label, so "subminute" covers BOTH
#              subminute_5m and subminute_15m; an exact label ("subminute_5m")
#              covers only itself; "*" covers every sleeve.
#   * LO-HI  — ask band, half-open (LO, HI] exactly like the strategy's entry band
#              (0.65, 0.85]: an ask of exactly LO trades, exactly HI is skipped.
# Malformed rules (wrong field count, blank coin/sleeve, non-numeric or
# inverted/out-of-[0,1] band) are IGNORED with a WARNING so one typo can neither
# wipe the spec nor fail closed into "skip everything". Applies in BOTH DRY and
# LIVE (unlike LATE_WINDOW_SKIP): this removes a cohort whose EDGE was refuted,
# so the paper stream must stop booking it too. No reserve, no POST, window NOT
# consumed (the next second re-evaluates), just an `ask_band_skip` signal. Kill
# switch = unset the var + restart.
#
# Canonical pin (2026-07-20 live-ledger study): SOL's 0.65-0.85 marginal-
# favorite band broke with a sharp boundary at the 07-17 halt. SOL clean fills
# (slip >= -0.01) went WR 87.3% -> 69.5%, +6.85c/$ -> -20.44c/$, +$38.77 ->
# -$15.26 (the window's single largest loss driver), while ETH (86.0 -> 88.4%)
# and BTC (84.2 -> 90.9%) HELD in the SAME band on the SAME days; holding ask
# fixed, SOL's same-price WR fell 84.1 -> 61.0% vs ETH 81.4 -> 83.8%, so it is
# not a price-mix artifact. Entries were statistically unchanged (offset, ask,
# model_p, model-market gap) and the Chainlink SOL feed was cleared — diagnosis
# is adverse selection on a thin marginal band. Damage is localized to SOL
# subminute_5m (n35, WR 68.6%) + subminute_15m (n6, WR 16.7%); SOL ask >= 0.85
# (100% WR) is HEALTHY and MUST keep trading — which is why the pin names the
# sleeve and the band, not the coin.
# [2026-07-21: operator override — 4-coin FULL size, no SOL gate.
# install_remote.sh SCRUBS this key from the live env on every deploy
# (remove_env_line) so a stale hand-added band can never linger and silently
# suppress a live cohort.]
# CRYPTOBOT_ASK_BAND_SKIP=SOL:subminute:0.65-0.85
#
# ⚠️ PRE-REGISTERED RE-ENABLE CRITERION — do NOT restore the band by feel. The
# effect is believed partly transient (SOL flip-rate already fell 29.6% ->
# 14.8%), so re-enable ONLY after a forward window of >= 3 CONSECUTIVE days OR
# >= 60 clean bets (whichever comes first) in which BOTH hold:
#     (a) band win-rate >= 80%, AND
#     (b) daily flip-rate <= 15% on EVERY day of the window.
# Both are computed from the `ask_band_skip` signals rows joined to the ledger:
# win-rate over clean fills (slip >= -0.01) in the band; flip-rate as the share
# of bets where the spot direction at window open reversed by settlement —
# ledger `window_open_spot` vs `strike_price` vs `won_up`. Re-enabling = simply
# unsetting the var; grade the counterfactual FIRST from the skipped cohort
# (every skipped entry keeps a full signals row, so avoided-PnL is computable
# without ever placing the bet).
#
# Fix 3b — fast-requote for flicker rejects (flag-gated, DEFAULT OFF =
# byte-identical). 3a skips a doomed POST; 3b targets the complementary ~8%
# "flicker" bucket where the book vanishes then flickers BACK a few hundred ms
# after a no_liquidity reject. When ENABLED, such a reject arms ONE bounded
# fast-requote for that (coin, interval, window, side); a dedicated short-cadence
# scheduler job (its OWN connection + the same OrderClient/book source) drains it
# ~DELAY_MS later: re-read the freshest book, re-run the sleeve BAND check on the
# fresh ask, re-derive the walked limit + anchored FAK pad, reserve a fresh
# attempt (the uniq active-slot index still serializes a race → clean drop), and
# POST once. A fill consumes the window (one-bet-per-market); a reject is terminal
# and arms no second requote. NO inline sleep runs on the tick thread. Only
# no_liquidity rejects arm — never auth/market_closed/insufficient_funds/
# venue_unavailable. Never fires after window_end.
# ARMED LIVE 2026-07-22 (operator order): tick-forensics on a SOL 15m window
# (5 no_liquidity attempts, 01:59:30-51 UTC) showed the exact target pattern —
# refills of $5-17 at <=limit flickering back 4-9s after the reject, aliased
# away by the 1 Hz sampler. The flag is the operator's manually-added key in
# /etc/cryptobot.env (install_remote does NOT pin it); grade its converts via
# the requote telemetry after a few days. Defaults (400ms delay, 1 attempt)
# left unchanged.
# CRYPTOBOT_FAST_REQUOTE_ENABLED=0
# Wait after the reject before the requote fires (drives the item delay AND the
# drain job's cadence).
# CRYPTOBOT_FAST_REQUOTE_DELAY_MS=400
# Max fast-requotes per (coin, interval, window, side). 1 = one extra shot.
# CRYPTOBOT_FAST_REQUOTE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=1
#
# Retry adverse-dip gate (operator 2026-07-24; flag-gated, DEFAULT OFF =
# byte-identical, backtest parity preserved). The per-second FAK retry
# (V2_REJECT_RETRY) re-enters a rejected offset window with NO adverse-dip
# fence, so it fills the cheap-refill cohort the fast-requote's
# FAST_REQUOTE_MIN_DELTA gate blocks — ground truth (era 2026-07-21..24): that
# cohort is the -EV maker-pull "chase" (14 next-tick fills, -$6.26; worst losers
# filled well BELOW limit, e.g. BTC 0.58 vs limit 0.69). When ON, the entry path
# skips re-entry on a rejected offset window whose FRESH ask has dipped below
# rejected_limit + FAST_REQUOTE_MIN_DELTA (reuses that -0.02 threshold); a
# flicker-back at/above the limit still fills (the +EV cohort is kept). Does NOT
# disable V2_REJECT_RETRY (backtest parity) — it gates adverse re-entry in front
# of it. ⚠️ Flag ON deliberately diverges retry reachability: re-baseline the
# v2/backtest parity suite + Fable review before arming live.
# CRYPTOBOT_RETRY_DIP_GATE_ENABLED=0
#
# GC tuning (latency finding #6; flag-gated, DEFAULT OFF = byte-identical).
# Boot pins a large permanently-live heap (RF/HGB/checkpoint artifacts + the
# LUT + the pandas/sklearn import graphs); stock CPython gen-2 passes re-scan
# ALL of it with the GIL held (plausibly 30-150ms on the box), landing at
# arbitrary points on the tick/stop path — including between a decision and
# its order POST. When ON: one gc.collect() + gc.freeze() after boot moves
# that heap into the permanent generation (never re-scanned again), the
# generation thresholds are raised to GEN0/GEN1/GEN2 (defaults 50000/20/20),
# and an explicit off-tick gc.collect() every COLLECT_SECONDS runs on the
# scheduler pool (wal_checkpoint pattern; 0 disables just the job) to bound
# memory creep. ⚠️ WATCH RSS for a day after arming — freeze + raised
# thresholds trade memory for latency on the 2GB box, and a frozen boot LUT
# later hot-swapped by the 30-min reload keeps its frozen copy alive
# (one-time, bounded, memory-only). Kill switch: unset (or 0) restores stock
# CPython GC exactly.
# CRYPTOBOT_GC_TUNING=1
# CRYPTOBOT_GC_GEN0_THRESHOLD=50000
# CRYPTOBOT_GC_GEN1_THRESHOLD=20
# CRYPTOBOT_GC_GEN2_THRESHOLD=20
# CRYPTOBOT_GC_COLLECT_SECONDS=60
# GC pause telemetry — INDEPENDENT flag so a before (telemetry on, tuning
# off) vs after (both on) can be measured: a gc.callbacks hook logs any
# collection pause >= 10ms ("gc_pause ..." in scanner logs).
# CRYPTOBOT_GC_PAUSE_TELEMETRY=1
#
# CLOB signing-pool warmth ping (latency finding #8; DEFAULT ON at 20s).
# Between orders the order/signing pool's only steady traffic is the 60s
# readiness balance read vs the pool's keepalive_expiry=65s — a 5s margin —
# and a readiness fire delayed >2s is dropped by the scheduler
# (misfire_grace_time), opening a ~120s gap that guarantees the socket
# expires so the next order POST pays a cold DNS+TCP+TLS handshake
# (~20-40ms) inside post_ms (httpcore never resumes TLS sessions). The
# clob_ping scheduler job fires a lightweight unauthenticated GET /ok on the
# SAME pool at this cadence, skipping itself when any pool traffic landed in
# the last 40s (the ping only fires after >=40s of pool silence — outside any
# active-trading band, still safely inside keepalive_expiry=65s at the 20s
# cadence) and using a 3s per-request timeout so a hung /ok can't pin a
# scheduler-pool worker. Off the decision path entirely; only wired when an
# OrderClient exists. Boot logs one "clob_ping warmth guard: active|inert"
# line — "inert" means the skip-guard response hook failed to install and
# every ping fires unconditionally. Kill switch: 0 disables the job AND the
# pool response hook — byte-identical to the pre-ping runtime.
# CRYPTOBOT_CLOB_PING_SECONDS=20
#
# On-chain miss forensics (operator order 2026-07-30, DEFAULT ON). Every
# missed trade must be explained from CHAIN evidence, not inferred. A 5-min
# scheduler job walks each new venue `no_liquidity` reject, joins it to
# live_order_attempts for the exact token we sent (the recorder is tokenless
# and Gamma has purged these markets — that join is the ONLY token source),
# resolves the complement token from the CLOB, and reads the trade tape:
#   FASTER_TAKER  a print inside the LEVEL BAND (from the ask we saw up to our
#                 limit, +-0.5c) within the venue-match window
#                 => the quote was REAL and another taker got there first
#   REPRICED_ONLY prints exist but all OUTSIDE the band => our level never traded
#   MAKER_CANCEL  no print at all => the resting order was withdrawn
#   PENDING       fetch failed / too fresh — retried next fire
#   UNRESOLVED    the venue no longer exposes both tokens (terminal)
# The band's LOWER bound is as load-bearing as the upper: a print far below the
# ask we saw is a different level of the book (usually the mint-matched
# complement of a trade deep on the other side), and counting it convicts a
# miss no speed could have won — 91.7% FASTER_TAKER unbanded vs the
# hand-verified 84% banded, over the first 48 rejects.
# Two more corrections are load-bearing, both established on 2026-07-30:
# (1) MINT-MATCH — an ask on token T prints either as a taker BUY of T at p OR
# a taker SELL of the complement at 1-p, and testing one shape loses half the
# evidence; (2) SETTLEMENT LAG — data-api/block timestamps run ~+3s AFTER the
# venue matched (calibrated on 106 of our own fills), so without subtracting it
# every rival print reads as LATE and a lost race looks like a late refill. The
# lag is re-calibrated from our own recent fills every 6h and the value used is
# stored per row in miss_forensics.lag_s_used.
# Results land on the Subminute tab: a per-miss verdict chip + a 7-day
# aggregate strip whose "speed prize" line (FASTER_TAKER would-win WR vs the
# break-even WR its own limit implies) is the metric that decides whether
# latency investment is ever worth anything. It was ~zero on 2026-07-30
# (78.9% vs 76.1%) — this panel re-checks that continuously.
# Strictly off the decision path: reads subminute_fills/live_order_attempts,
# writes only miss_forensics, every exception swallowed with a WARN, per-run
# HTTP/RPC call counts hard-capped so a venue outage costs a bounded number of
# calls and then leaves rows PENDING. Polymarket-only: the predict.fun paper
# unit shares this core but its fills are not on Polygon, and main.py gates the
# job on CRYPTOBOT_VENUE=polymarket. Reads POLY_FUNDER (to exclude our OWN
# prints — a sibling attempt on the same window can genuinely fill) and, when
# set, POLYGON_RPC_URL for the rival maker address off the OrderFilled log.
# Kill switch: 0 registers no job at all.
# CRYPTOBOT_MISS_FORENSICS_ENABLED=1
# CRYPTOBOT_MISS_FORENSICS_SECONDS=300

# ---- Fast-trigger entry path (operator 2026-07-30, DEFAULT ON) --------------
# The lever the forensic above pointed at. 84% of our misses went to a FASTER
# TAKER, median 1.0s before we arrived, ~5x our size, at exactly our quoted ask.
# The POST path is already at the venue floor (sign ~1ms, POST ~300ms of which
# 250ms is the taker delay every taker pays), so the ONLY reclaimable latency is
# trigger-to-decision: the scanner samples once per second on a boundary-aligned
# tick, so an ask that becomes fillable mid-second waits ~500ms on average
# before we look at it. Two extra trigger rungs close that gap:
#   * SWEEP — an APScheduler job every CRYPTOBOT_FAST_TRIGGER_MS (clamped
#     >=100ms). Outside a qualifying offset window it returns after pure integer
#     math over the sleeves' offset sets, so it is ~free ~90% of the time.
#   * EVENT — the WS book mirror fires an ask-side callback and a coalescing
#     worker re-evaluates within ~20ms of the push. Needs
#     CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_ENABLED=1 (Polymarket only today — predict.fun's
#     market-keyed mirror exposes no ask-update hook yet, so PF runs the sweep
#     rung alone).
# Both converge on the TICK'S OWN single-cell evaluation (same scoring at the
# same integer offset_sec, same book resolver, same _commit_cell), so band,
# gate, V2_EDGE_CAP, sizing/caps/DD-brake, one-per-window dedup, the
# WindowDecider same-offset dedup, first-attempt-only and multifill all bind
# unchanged — a fast-path no_liquidity reject spends the side exactly like the
# tick's would. The fast rungs never spend a REST book call (push/cache only)
# and write NO rows unless something places or rejects. A fast scan and the
# tick's per-cell commit are single-flighted: the tick takes the lock BLOCKING
# (never skipped), a fast rung takes it NON-BLOCKING and abandons the scan.
# Grade it: subminute_fills.trigger_src IN ('fast_sweep','fast_event') vs 'tick'
# (fast-vs-tick realized c/$), and the FASTER_TAKER share in miss_forensics.
# Kill switches: ENABLED=0 registers no job, no WS callback, and the tick takes
# no lock (byte-identical); EVENT_ENABLED=0 keeps the sweep, drops the WS rung.
# CRYPTOBOT_FAST_TRIGGER_ENABLED=1
# CRYPTOBOT_FAST_TRIGGER_MS=250
# CRYPTOBOT_FAST_TRIGGER_EVENT_ENABLED=1

# ---- Book recorders (BOTH venues) — RETIRED 2026-08-02, CODE DELETED 08-04 ---
# The self-hosted pmdata-mode Polymarket book recorder (book-recorder.service,
# data/book_recorder/) and the predict.fun calibration recorder
# (predictfun-book-recorder.service, data/predictfun_book_recorder/) are gone:
# units, modules and every CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_RECORDER_* / CRYPTOBOT_PREDICTFUN_
# RECORDER_* key. Nothing reads them. install_remote.sh tears both units down
# idempotently. Scrub any surviving CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_RECORDER_ENABLED /
# CRYPTOBOT_PREDICTFUN_RECORDER_ENABLED line from /etc/cryptobot.env by hand —
# they are now inert, but they are also a lie.
# The recorders' only consumer was the book-execution pool rebuild, killed
# 2026-07-31 with book_depth_index and the pmdata ledgers, and both venues'
# collected history was deleted 2026-08-02. Recover from git history if wanted.
# ⚠️ NOT this: CRYPTOBOT_BOOK_WS_* above is the LIVE-TRADING book feed, a
# different thing entirely, and stays armed.

# ---- RTDS crypto-price recorder — RETIRED 2026-08-01 ------------------------
# RTDS recorder retired 2026-08-01, prereg abandoned ungraded by operator order.
# The unit, the module and every CRYPTOBOT_RTDS_RECORDER_* key are gone; nothing
# reads them. Scrub any surviving CRYPTOBOT_RTDS_RECORDER_ENABLED line from
# /etc/cryptobot.env by hand — it is now inert, but it is also a lie.

# ---- Venue selection (predict.fun support) ----------------------------------
# CRYPTOBOT_VENUE picks the trading venue. UNSET or "polymarket" (default) is
# byte-identical to every current behavior. "predictfun" swaps in the
# cryptobot_predictfun.* adapters at the market-discovery / order-book / order /
# settlement seams AND narrows the default scan universe to predict.fun's
# BTC/ETH/BNB crypto up-down markets (no SOL/XRP). The deployed DRY paper
# instance pins CRYPTOBOT_COINS=BTC,ETH on top of that default (operator order
# 2026-07-21 — BNB out of the paper universe; the recorder still records BNB).
# ⚠️ The live Polymarket box MUST leave this unset (or =polymarket).
#
# ⚠️ BOOT-STRICT since 2026-07-28 (Phase 2). An unrecognized value used to log a
# warning and FALL BACK to polymarket — which means a typo here would have
# traded REAL MONEY on the wrong venue. It now REFUSES TO BOOT. Valid values are
# exactly the venue registry's keys: polymarket, predictfun, kalshi. "kalshi" is
# registered so the map is total but its adapter is a stub — pinning it fails
# loudly at first use rather than trading somewhere else.
# CRYPTOBOT_VENUE=polymarket
#
# predict.fun REST + auth (ONLY read on the predictfun venue / its recorder; the
# polymarket path never reads these). PREDICTFUN_API_BASE is env-switchable so
# the PUBLIC testnet can be used for integration tests without a key; mainnet
# requires PREDICTFUN_API_KEY (a GET 401s without it; sent as an `x-api-key`
# header — 2026-07-21 mainnet probe: `Authorization: Bearer <key>` 401s, Bearer
# is the /auth JWT for trading endpoints). Server budget is 240 requests/min
# per key, SHARED across every process using it (recorder + paper scanner).
# PREDICTFUN_PRIVATE_KEY signs EIP-712 orders on the LIVE path ONLY — DRY mode
# + the book recorder never read it (DRY-without-creds is supported).
# ⚠️ The real API key is set ONLY in /etc/cryptobot.env on the box — it must
# never be written into any git-tracked file (this example stays EMPTY).
# PREDICTFUN_API_BASE=https://api.predict.fun/v1
#   (testnet, public, no key: https://api-testnet.predict.fun/v1)
# PREDICTFUN_API_KEY=
# PREDICTFUN_PRIVATE_KEY=
# The "Predict account" (Kernel smart wallet). predict.fun UI accounts custody
# collateral on a Kernel smart account; the Privy-exported key controls a
# DIFFERENT owner EOA that signs for it. Set to the smart-account address for
# UI accounts (orders get maker=<this>, /auth uses the predict-account flow,
# balance reads target it). Leave EMPTY for external-wallet (EOA-only) accounts.
# PREDICTFUN_PREDICT_ACCOUNT=
# PREDICTFUN_CHAIN_ID=56        # 56=BNB mainnet, 97=BNB testnet
# Per-market taker-fee fallback (bps) when a market omits feeRateBps. 200 (=2%)
# observed on every probed market. The TENT fee SHAPE (feeRateBps/10000 *
# min(p,1-p)) is applied in code; this is only the fallback bps. NOT the
# Polymarket POLY_FEE_THETA parabola.
# PREDICTFUN_DEFAULT_FEE_RATE_BPS=200

# The predict.fun book recorder that used to be documented here was retired with
# the Polymarket one — see the book-recorder retirement block above.

# ---- predict.fun DRY paper scanner (SECOND instance, flag-gated) ------------
# A second `python -m cryptobot` process (cryptobot-predictfun.service) running
# the SAME strategy stack against predict.fun's BTC/ETH up-down markets,
# PAPER ONLY: DRY mode, $100 paper bankroll, its OWN SQLite file
# (data/cryptobot_predictfun.db — never data/cryptobot.db; latches/accounting/
# operator state are single-venue, sharing would corrupt the LIVE bot; the
# unit's ReadWritePaths carve out ONLY that DB's three files, so the live DB
# is read-only in its mount namespace), its own
# loopback dashboard on 8801, and PREDICTFUN_PRIVATE_KEY forced empty (order
# placement structurally impossible). Its per-key env overrides live in
# /etc/cryptobot-predictfun.env, REGENERATED by install_remote.sh every deploy
# (a later EnvironmentFile= wins per-key over this shared file) — do not edit
# that file by hand.
# Paper universe = BTC,ETH ONLY (operator order 2026-07-21): BNB is OUT of the
# scan universe — it scored zero paper bets anyway (no BNB-trained model slice,
# rf_slice_missing every tick). The predict.fun book RECORDER still records
# BNB books (its coin set is untouched — calibration data keeps flowing).
# Default OFF. Arm by pinning =1 here + redeploy; install_remote.sh then
# enables+restarts the unit (unit-level gating only — main.py has no self-exit
# on this flag). Operator steps after first boot: (1) `ssh -L 8801:127.0.0.1:8801`
# and press Start once (a fresh DB seeds STOPPED_PROCESSING).
# ⚠️ MEMORY: do NOT arm on the current ~4 GB box — this loads the full 614 MB+
# artifact stack next to the live unit's 3300M ceiling. Upsize to >= 8 GB first
# (the unit's MemoryMax sits below the live unit's so the OOM-killer prefers
# the paper bot, but arming on a small box still risks the live process).
# ⚠️ Paper bets need the mainnet PREDICTFUN_API_KEY above; without it every
# market GET 401s and the instance idles (fail-closed).
# CRYPTOBOT_PREDICTFUN_DRY_ENABLED=1

# ---- predict.fun LIVE mode (REAL MONEY — operator-armed) --------------------
# Flips the SECOND scanner instance from the paper-DRY variant to REAL-MONEY
# trading: install_remote.sh regenerates /etc/cryptobot-predictfun.env with
# DRY_RUN=false, the LIVE artifact (wallet_default_modes LIVE), a FRESH live
# DB (data/predictfun_live/ — the paper DB is left untouched as the
# calibration baseline), signing key + telegram INHERITED from this shared
# file, and a systemd drop-in adding OnFailure paging. The flag lives HERE
# (shared env) so it survives every deploy; unsetting it + redeploying reverts
# the instance to paper and removes the drop-in.
# ⚠️ PREREQUISITE: the staged
# validation CLI must have PASSED on this box first —
#   cbot-predictfun-live-validation --stage preflight|auth|build|reject|order
# — the submit wire (POST /v1/orders + /auth JWT) was implemented 2026-07-23
# from the venue docs and is only PROVEN by that protocol. Requires
# PREDICTFUN_PRIVATE_KEY (+ PREDICTFUN_PREDICT_ACCOUNT for UI accounts) above.
# CRYPTOBOT_PREDICTFUN_LIVE=1
# OPTIONAL. Bet sizing NEVER uses this — stakes size off the SCANNED on-chain
# collateral balance every tick (operator order 2026-07-23), so deposits/
# withdrawals take effect automatically. This only seeds the DD brake/halt
# accounting basis + dashboard display + the stale-balance-cache sizing
# fallback (default 100).
# CRYPTOBOT_PREDICTFUN_LIVE_BANKROLL=100
